<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Arabia and the Gulf</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Awsan</h1><p class="st-meta">750 BCE – 650 BCE (approx.) · capital Hagar Yahirr</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A short-lived south Arabian kingdom in Wadi Markha whose power over the coast was broken by Saba in the 7th century BCE.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Awsan lay in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wadi-markha">Wadi Markha</a>, south-west of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/incense">incense</a> valleys, with its capital at Hagar Yahirr. Known mainly from Sabaean inscriptions, it seems to have risen in the 8th century BCE and controlled territory towards the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-aden">Gulf of Aden</a> coast and its harbours.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Very little is known of its internal life. Its wealth probably came from coastal trade and the routes linking the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabian-sea">Arabian Sea</a> with the inland <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/incense">incense</a> kingdoms. Later Awsanite inscriptions show kings who were honoured as gods after death, an unusual practice in south <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The Sabaean ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karibil-watar">Karib'il Watar</a> destroyed Awsan in the 7th century BCE, according to his great inscription at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sirwah">Sirwah</a>, killing thousands and handing its lands to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-saba">Kingdom of Saba</a> and its allies. A smaller Awsan reappeared later, and the Greek name of the Ausanitic coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-africa">East Africa</a> recalls it.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-awsan.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Awsan" width="320" height="211"><figcaption>Image: Mnohohrishnyi · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kingdom_of_Awsan_locator_wadis_settlemetns_zoomed.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>750 BCE – 650 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/7th-century-bce">7th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Hagar Yahirr</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>South Arabian polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Ancient South Arabian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/yemen">Yemen</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Ausan</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-700&amp;focus=kingdom-of-awsan" aria-label="Kingdom of Awsan on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5933 1608 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Awsan lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6237 1859h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6253 1864h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M6253 1864h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Yemen. <a href="/atlas?year=-700&amp;focus=kingdom-of-awsan">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

